  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A prism of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and another prism of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are stuck together (as shown in the figure). <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> depend on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the wavelength of light, according to the relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p>The wavelength for which rays incident at any angle on the interface <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> pass through without bending at that interface will be ____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nm</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0134_f349853ca873.png\" style=\"width: 293px; height: 195px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "600",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For no bending, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math><br />On solving,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>"
  }
}